---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PostList from '../components/PostList.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/display-picture.jpg';
import { SITE, getPosts } from '../site';

const posts = await getPosts();

const numbers = [
  { value: '10+', label: 'years building and running production infrastructure' },
  { value: '10k+', label: 'learners on the Kubernetes platform I look after now' },
  { value: '30%+', label: 'cut in infrastructure cost when we moved that platform to autoscaling Kubernetes' },
  { value: '900+', label: 'lifts monitored by Franz, an IoT product I helped build from scratch' },
];

const cases = [
  {
    tag: 'Reliability',
    title: 'The 200-user wall',
    summary:
      'A load test kept stalling at about 170 of 200 users, and every log looked fine. It took ten runs to find out that autoscaling was reconfiguring the load balancer in the middle of the test. Now all 200 get in.',
    href: '/2026-10-28/the-200-user-wall/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Recovery',
    title: 'Backups someone has actually restored',
    summary:
      'We had backups, but nobody had ever restored from one. I wrote the runbook and a script that works out which backups you need, and then we timed a real restore of the main databases.',
    href: '/2026-10-29/a-backup-counts-once-restored/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
  {
    tag: 'AI agents',
    title: 'Letting Claude near our infrastructure',
    summary:
      'We wanted an AI agent to look into infrastructure problems without borrowing anyone’s access. So it got its own identity, short-lived credentials, a sandbox, and a hook that blocks anything we haven’t allowed.',
    href: '/2026-10-29/guardrails-for-ai-agents/',
    cta: 'Read the post',
  },
  {
    tag: 'IoT',
    title: 'Franz, from nothing to 900+ lifts',
    summary:
      'A lift-monitoring product with its own hardware, firmware, edge software and cloud, built by one team at the same time. I built the edge software and the over-the-air updates. We had a working MVP in under six months.',
    href: '/work/#relayr-senior',
    cta: 'More on my work page',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">Syed Usman · Infrastructure &amp; DevOps engineer · Berlin</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m Syed. I build and run infrastructure in Berlin.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I’ve spent about ten years on platforms that other engineers depend on. Right now that’s a Kubernetes platform
        for more than 10,000 learners. Before that it was industrial IoT, including sensors in over 900 lifts. Lately
        I’ve also been working out how to let AI agents near real infrastructure safely. I write here about things that
        broke, and what I got wrong on the way to fixing them.
      </p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/2026-10-28/the-200-user-wall/">Read “The 200-user wall”</a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="/work/">See my work</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-portrait">
      <Image src={portrait} alt="Syed Usman, smiling, on a balcony above Berlin" width={480} height={600} fit="cover" position="top" loading="eager" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="numbers">
    <h2 id="numbers" class="section-label">A few numbers</h2>
    <ul class="numbers">
      {
        numbers.map((n) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{n.value}</strong>
            <span>{n.label}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="selected">
    <h2 id="selected" class="section-label">Selected work</h2>
    <div class="cases">
      {
        cases.map((c) => (
          <article class="case">
            <p class="case-tag">{c.tag}</p>
            <h3>{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="case-summary">{c.summary}</p>
            <a class="case-link" href={c.href}>
              {c.cta} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="writing">
    <div class="narrow">
    <h2 id="writing" class="section-label">Writing</h2>
    <PostList posts={posts.slice(0, 5)} />
    {posts.length > 5 && <p><a class="case-link" href="/writing/">All writing →</a></p>}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="hello">
    <div class="narrow cta">
    <h2 id="hello">Hiring for platform work?</h2>
    <p>
      If you’re building a platform or infrastructure team, I’d like to hear what you’re working on. Email is the best
      way to reach me.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
